From 8cd4c225a008e6aa67806bd032d071ba4c3e4910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:40:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] build_features: indicate WNM, MBO and proxy ARP

A program that configures hostapd cannot tell whether the build parses
bss_transition, wnm_sleep_mode and wnm_sleep_mode_no_keys (CONFIG_WNM_AP),
mbo (CONFIG_MBO) or proxy_arp (CONFIG_PROXYARP); a build without one
refuses the whole configuration at such a line, as an unknown item.
Answer "wnm-ap", "mbo" and "proxyarp" in has_feature(), so that
`hostapd -vwnm-ap` and the others tell it.

CONFIG_WNM alone does not tell it: wpa_supplicant's Makefile sets
CONFIG_WNM for CONFIG_MBO, so a multicall wpad-basic defines CONFIG_WNM
but not CONFIG_WNM_AP, and refuses bss_transition.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 src/utils/build_features.h | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/src/utils/build_features.h
+++ b/src/utils/build_features.h
@@ -79,6 +79,18 @@ static inline int has_feature(const char
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "robust-av-scs"))
 		return 1;
 #endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_WNM_AP
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "wnm-ap"))
+		return 1;
+#endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_MBO
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "mbo"))
+		return 1;
+#endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_PROXYARP
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "proxyarp"))
+		return 1;
+#endif
 	return 0;
 }
 
